# Optional. Pl@ntNet and Gemini both ship a built-in key as a fallback, so this
# file is only needed to rotate them without a code change.
#
# Set values locally by copying this file to .env, and on Vercel under
# Project Settings → Environment Variables. Any value set there overrides the
# built-in value. Leave a line blank to use the built-in value.
#
# Both keys are browser-visible by design — this site builds to a single static
# file with no server to proxy through. Pl@ntNet restricts its key by domain
# (authorized origins in the Pl@ntNet dashboard). The Gemini key has NO origin
# lock, so it can be spent by anyone who reads the published source until it is
# rotated — treat it as disposable.
# SECURITY — READ THIS FIRST (after Google's exposure notice, 2026-09-28):
# A `VITE_*` value is PUBLIC by design: Vite inlines it into the JS bundle that
# every visitor downloads. Setting keys in Vercel env does NOT hide them — it
# only lets you ROTATE without a code change. So:
#   1. ROTATE a leaked key immediately (AI Studio → Keys → delete + create new;
#      Pl@ntNet dashboard → regenerate). The old key dies on next redeploy.
#   2. RESTRICT the Gemini key in AI Studio to the "Generative Language API"
#      only, so a leaked key can't spend other Google services. Set a quota cap.
#   3. Pl@ntNet: keep the domain allowlist tight (production domain only).
# True hiding needs the Supabase Edge Function relay (`supabase/functions/identify`,
# plan §11): keys live in Supabase secrets, the browser never sees them. Until then, treat both keys
# as disposable and rotate on any exposure notice.
# NOTE: unset vars don't just fail closed at runtime — Vite folds them at BUILD
# time and the unconfigured vendor path is eliminated from the bundle entirely
# (verified: no key bytes, no endpoint strings). So set vars BEFORE build/deploy
# on Vercel, and redeploy after any rotation.
#
# SECURE PATH (recommended): deploy the relay, then set ONLY this in .env/Vercel.
# No vendor key in the bundle at all — rotation happens in Supabase Dashboard
# (Edge Functions → Secrets) with zero redeploy.
#   Vercel + local .env:
#   VITE_IDENTIFY_PROXY_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/identify
#   Supabase secrets (Dashboard or `supabase secrets set`):
#   PLANTNET_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, GEMINI_MODEL, ALLOWED_ORIGINS
VITE_IDENTIFY_PROXY_URL=
VITE_PLANTNET_API_KEY=
# Gemini is used only as the fallback when Pl@ntNet's daily quota is reached.
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Model used for the fallback. 3.1-flash-lite is the working free-tier model on
# this key (3.6-flash's quota ran dry and 3.5-flash-lite mangles the JSON
# response). Model names churn often, so if identification breaks, check this
# value first.
VITE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
# Supabase (public reads; RLS guards everything — anon key is public by design,
# service key stays out of this repo forever).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xnonklducighcdbtlbhw.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Cloudinary delivery (public cloud name only — building image URLs needs it).
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=